TRADEMARK

CC BY 4.0 grants no trademark rights (section 2(b)(2) of the license). The
name "Conductress", the keyhole-C mark, and the lockups in this directory
identify the Conductress project. They are unregistered marks used by the
project since 2026.

You may use the name and mark to refer to Conductress: in articles, talks,
compatibility statements, package listings, and links to the project. You may
adapt the artwork under CC BY 4.0, for example to produce a new size or file
format for the project.

Please do not use the name or mark, or anything confusingly similar, as the
name or logo of a fork, a derivative product, a service, or an unrelated
project, and do not use them in a way that implies the Conductress project
produced, endorsed, or supports something it did not. A fork should choose its
own name and mark. This is the same convention most open-source projects
follow, and it is what lets "Conductress" continue to mean one thing.

THIRD-PARTY MARKS

The hexagon shape references the Valkey logo, which belongs to LF Projects,
LLC. The Valkey logo itself is not included here and is not covered by this
license. The six-band rainbow palette in brand/pride/ is an homage to the
1977 Apple logo; no Apple mark is included and none is claimed.
